[00:00.31]Lesson 6 | 第6课
[00:01.51]The sporting spirit | 体育精神
[00:07.64]How does the writer describe sport at the international level? | 作者如何描述国际层面的体育运动？
[00:14.09]I am always amazed when I hear people saying that sport creates goodwill between the nations, and that if only the common peoples of the world could meet one another at football or cricket, they would have no inclination to meet on the battlefield. | 我听到人们说体育能在国家之间创造亲善感情，还说只要世界各地的普通民众能在足球场或板球场上相遇，他们就不会再有在战场上相遇的念头，对此我总是感到惊愕。
[00:30.32]Even if one didn't know from concrete examples (the 1936 Olympic Games, for instance) that international sporting contests lead to orgies of hatred, one could deduce it from general principles. | 即使不从具体事例（例如1936年奥运会）中知道国际体育比赛会导致疯狂的仇恨，人们也可以从一般原则中推出这一点。
[00:45.53]Nearly all the sports practised nowadays are competitive. | 如今开展的所有体育运动几乎都是竞技性的。
[00:49.40]You play to win, and the game has little meaning unless you do your utmost to win. | 参加比赛就是为了取胜，如果不拼命去赢，比赛就没有什么意义了。
[00:55.66]On the village green, where you pick up sides and no feeling of local patriotism is involved, it is possible to play simply for the fun and exercise: but as soon as a the question of prestige arises, as soon as you feel that you and some larger unit will be disgraced if you lose, the most savage combative instincts are aroused. | 在乡间的草坪上，你随意挑选参赛的双方，不带任何地方爱国情绪，那样才可能单纯地为了娱乐和锻炼而赛一场；然而一旦涉及到声望问题，一旦你感觉到你和一个较大的团体会因输掉比赛而丢脸时，最野蛮的争斗本能就会被激发起来。
[01:19.34]Anyone who has played even in a school football match knows this. | 凡是参加过哪怕是学校足球赛的人都知道这一点。
[01:23.62]At the international level, sport is frankly mimic warfare. | 在国际层面上，体育坦率地说是模拟战争。
[01:28.62]But the significant thing is not the behaviour of the players but the attitude of the spectators: | 但重要的不是运动员的行为，而是观众的态度，
[01:34.89]and, behind the spectators, of the nations who work themselves into furies over these absurd contests, | 以及观众背后那些国家的心态：这些国家在这些荒唐的比赛中如痴如狂，
[01:41.93]and seriously believe -- at any rate for short periods -- that running, jumping and kicking a ball are tests of national virtue. | 并且煞有介事地相信——至少在短时间内——跑步、跳跃和踢球是对民族美德的检验。
